.TH XSTART 1 "31 October 2026" "amix-base"
.SH NAME
xstart \- start X on this machine's display
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xstart
[
.B \-n
] [
.B \-xdm
|
.B \-dtlogin
] [
.BI : N
] [
.IR W x H
] [
.IB key = value
\&... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xstart
starts an X session on the display card, mode and depth that
.B /etc/display
names (see
.BR display (4)),
with the X server and arguments the card's file in
.B /etc/display.d
gives (see
.BR display.d (4)).
An argument changes one field of
.B /etc/display
for this session only:
.IR W x H
is the mode, and
.BR card= ,
.BR mode= ,
.BR depth= ,
.B session=
and
.B monsw=
the others.
.BI : N
is the display number (default
.BR :0 ).
.PP
In order,
.B xstart
finds the card (with
.BR "card auto" ,
the first whose device answers, the chipset display last), checks the mode
and depth against the card's, raises the limits the card asks for, switches
the monitor to the card when the card shares it, and runs the server through
.B xinit
(X11R6's, else the system's) with the session:
.BR ~/.xsession ,
else
.BR ~/.xinitrc ,
else the
.B session
of
.BR /etc/display ,
else
.BR /usr/lib/amix/xsession .
The card's environment
.RB ( env )
reaches the server alone, through a small script
.B xstart
writes in
.B /tmp
and removes afterwards.
When the session ends, the monitor is switched back; when the server ended
on its own instead (it crashed or was killed), the card's
.B restore
command runs too.
.PP
The system's
.B startx
is still there and unchanged.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
say what would be run, and every mistake in
.B /etc/display
and the card files, and run nothing.
.TP
.B \-xdm \fR|\fP \-dtlogin
instead of a session, start X11R6's
.B xdm
or CDE's
.B dtlogin
with the same server line; the boot step
.B S95display
does this when
.B /etc/display
says
.B start xdm
or
.BR "start dtlogin" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the session ran (with
.BR \-n :
when the files hold no mistake); 1 when the display cannot be set up (no
card answers, a mode or depth the card does not have, no server, no
.BR xinit );
2 on a usage mistake.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/display
the machine's choice.
.TP
.B /etc/display.d/*
the cards.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/amix/xsession
the default session.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR display (4),
.BR display.d (4)
.SH NOTES
The keyboard map under X is not yet derived from the console's
.BR /etc/default.kmap ;
a
.B ~/.Xmodmap
run from the session sets it.
